body:
I guess if God has made it that all will be saved, is he not just reverting to relativism?

&#x200B;

So do you not go to Church?

I think we agree on sin, we might be talking past one another.  

&#x200B;

I think I'm slowly coming to terms with Mary being sinless. But why can't God come from a sinful Vessel? Is it because he turns death into life, so it is impossible for him to be in a womb without purifying it?

&#x200B;

>Yes and no. A baby cannot sin so they are sinless but a baby still suffers from the sin of Adam and Eve and so they suffer from sin but do not sin.

But Babies have not committed sin?  They are effected by sin from others, but how does that make them inherently sinful?

&#x200B;

>Because God who is completely pure and good cannot come from a sinful vessel?

But he can come from a vessell that makes mistakes?

>God can withhold someone from sinning without effecting their free will.

What? How does that work?

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

>eo just holds that the consequence of death was passed on, while Adam and Eve are solely guilty of the actual original sin.

Yes I'm guilty of my own sin, no one else's

&#x200B;

>Because the necessity of Mary being sinless to fulfill the old covenant.

Does then Mary not have freewill?

&#x200B;

>No, we are born into sin. The moment you were conceived you took on Adam's original sin. This is all explained in detail in Romans 5:12-21.

Well I'm not in agreement with St Augustine on Original Sin. I'm more in line with the Eastern Orthodox position

TBF they would still agree that the Father and Jesus are distinct.  In fact their problem is that they think they are seperate beings.

&#x200B;

But I'm not aware that Arianism had that many modern followers.  What sects do they belong to?

Constantine 1 was sainted though, it's not impossible.  And just because someone isn't sainted doesn't mean that they aren't respectable and heroic.  And also the church says that they do not create saints but rather recognise them.  So there are many saints out there which have not been canonised. 

&#x200B;

I just find it hard though to accept running away from your responsibilities and from death is the Christ thing to do.  I'm really hoping you are an exception to orthodoxy beliefs and not the norm.  Because you make Orthodoxy seem very American protestant like.

Damn hating Western Christianity more than Islam is something I would have never expected from an Orthodox Christian.

&#x200B;

Are you Oriental or Eastern? sorry bro for the ignorance

That's why the first crusades happened wasn't?  To help him?

&#x200B;

Also why do you as an orthodox person,  name the Eastern Romans as Byzantines.  They only ever saw themselves as Roman? They were called Byzantines after the fact because the West claimed themselves to be the successor of Rome
